#=======================================================================
# Compiling Generate with gnu compiler                    
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Usage:                                                                
#   make <FORTRAN=gnu/intel/nvidia> <DEBUG=no/yes> <ASSERT=yes/no>      
#        <FCOMP=gfortran/ifort/nvfortran/mpif90/mpiifort/...>           
#        <PROF=no/yes> <REAL=double/single> <OMP=yes/no>                
#        <SORT=heap/quick> <clean>                                      
#                                                                       
# Notes:                                                                
#   1. The first item, for each of the options above, is the default.   
#   2. Target "clean" removes all compiled files and binaries.          
#                                                                       
# Examples:                                                             
#   make               - compile with gnu compiler                      
#   make FORTRAN=intel - compile with intel compiler                    
#   make DEBUG=yes     - compile with gnu compiler in debug mode        
#   make ASSERT=no     - compile without assert with gnu compiler       
#   make OMP=yes       - compile with gnu compiler for parallel Generate
#   make SORT=heap     - use heap-sort variant of sorting functions     
#   make clean         - remove all compiled files and binaries         
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------
